    "note": "Ruling 7 approved the body proportions as drafted. Ruling 8 applied the measured thigh/shin swap. Ruling 9 made the base root bone at the origin normative, with the pelvis parented to it. Ruling 10 approved +Y-along-bone."
  },
  "note": "APPROVED 2026-08-08, canon version 1.0, by the rulings recorded in docs/RULINGS-2026-08-08.md. Two numbers changed on the way in: the thigh is now 0.43 m and the shin 0.42 m (ruling 8, on measurements from two human-derived rigs), which moves the knee from y = 0.50 to y = 0.49 and moves nothing else. The root is a BASE BONE at the origin and the pelvis is parented to it (ruling 9), so a travelling clip carries locomotion on the root and the pelvis stays a body bone. These numbers are now painful to change: every retarget map, every calibration solve and every clip authored against this rig inherits them.",
